\section{Introduction and Covariant Foundations}

Astrophysical phenomena involving extreme gravitational fields require a fully
covariant treatment of spacetime and plasma dynamics. SMSE-v1 models these
systems using the $3+1$ ADM formalism of General Relativity.

The spacetime interval is
\begin{equation}
ds^2 = g_{\mu\nu} dx^\mu dx^\nu,
\end{equation}
with the $3+1$ decomposition
\begin{equation}
ds^2 = -\alpha^2 dt^2
+ \gamma_{ij} (dx^i + \beta^i dt)(dx^j + \beta^j dt),
\end{equation}
where $\alpha$ is the lapse, $\beta^i$ the shift vector, and $\gamma_{ij}$ the
spatial metric.

\section{Governing Equations of GRMHD}

Relativistic magnetized plasmas obey the conservation laws
\begin{align}
\nabla_\mu (\rho u^\mu) &= 0,\\
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} &= 0,
\end{align}
where $\rho$ is rest-mass density and $u^\mu$ the fluid 4-velocity.

The GRMHD energy-momentum tensor is
\begin{equation}
T^{\mu\nu}
=
(\rho h + b^2) u^\mu u^\nu
+
\left(p + \frac{b^2}{2}\right) g^{\mu\nu}
-
b^\mu b^\nu,
\end{equation}
with specific enthalpy
\begin{equation}
h = 1 + \frac{\epsilon}{c^2} + \frac{p}{\rho c^2}.
\end{equation}

